Important notes about connection:
1. Solder load cell wires DIRECTLY to HX711 Amplifier
2. Twist load cell wires to reduce noise
3. Load cell needs to be screwed in very tight and firm, with space in its casing/platforms to allow for deformation
4. Solder wires directly to HX711's Vcc, GND, and output connections, with wires plugged directly into Arduino's (D4 and D5) pins.


3D printed load cell housing that works well: https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:5448276
  Note: screw holes do not line up - current prototype just uses back hole. Thingiverse files include cad files,
        so could potentially modify file to fit our load cell for our final device


